# Elysium WowPacketParser (WPP)

**One unified WowPacketParser. Six independent client distributions. Multiple generations of World of Warcraft.**

Elysium WowPacketParser is a community-maintained collection of World of Warcraft packet analysis tools based on [TrinityCore's WowPacketParser](https://github.com/TrinityCore/WowPacketParser), with additional client-version research, experimental opcode discoveries, and independently maintained releases.

Elysium WPP offers two ways to work with World of Warcraft packets:

- **Elysium WPP All-in-One** — A unified parser supporting multiple World of Warcraft client families in one installation.
- **Individual Client WPPs** — Six independently maintained distributions for Retail, PTR, Classic Era, Burning Crusade Classic, Mists of Pandaria Classic, and WoW Forever.

Our goal is to preserve reliable packet analysis while expanding compatibility with newer World of Warcraft clients through authenticated protocol research.

---

## Official Releases

### Elysium WPP All-in-One v1.0.0

**Release:** `wpp.v1.0.0.rar`

The first official release of **Elysium WowPacketParser All-in-One**, combining TrinityCore-based client support with Elysium's additional Retail opcode research and experimental build recognition.

**Included capabilities:**

- Automatic client-build detection.
- Retail, PTR, Classic Era, BCC, and MoP Classic parser infrastructure.
- Experimental Retail 12.1.5.70961 recognition.
- Additional provisional Retail 70783 opcode mappings.
- 23 parser modules.
- Original WPP packet decoding and SQL generation.
- Original command-line interface and configuration functionality.
- .NET 10 Release build.
- 118 automated tests passed, 6 skipped, 0 failed.

**WoW Forever is not yet integrated into All-in-One.** Use the separate Forever WPP distribution.

### Individual Client Releases

Each supported client family has its own independently built and maintained WPP distribution.

| Distribution | Release / Naming Convention | Availability |
|---|---|---|
| All-in-One | `wpp.v1.0.0.rar` | Published |
| Retail | `retail_<build>_wpp` | Published |
| PTR | `ptr_12.1.7.70892_wpp` | Published |
| Classic Era | `classic_<build>_wpp` | Built and tested locally |
| Burning Crusade Classic | `bcc_<build>_wpp` | Built and tested locally |
| MoP Classic | `mopc_<build>_wpp` | Built and tested locally |
| Forever | `forever_<build>_wpp` | Built and tested locally |

Names containing `<build>` are naming patterns, not specific published release identifiers.

**Download the release matching your intended client, or use All-in-One when you want multiple supported client families in one installation.**

A release name identifying a client build does not, by itself, establish complete protocol compatibility with that build.

