## Supported World of Warcraft Clients

| Client | All-in-One | Individual WPP |
|---|---|---|
| Retail | Included | Available |
| PTR | Included through upstream version dispatch | Available |
| Classic Era | Included | Available locally |
| Burning Crusade Classic | Included | Available locally |
| Mists of Pandaria Classic | Included, known limitations | Available locally |
| World of Warcraft Forever | Not yet integrated | Available locally |

All-in-One uses a unified source tree and the original WPP client-version dispatch architecture.

Individual WPP distributions retain separate source directories, build environments, parser modules, and publishing workflows.

### Retail

| Client Build | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 12.1.5.70783 | Supported baseline | Verified SQL and parsed-text comparison for an authenticated PKT |
| 12.1.5.70961 | Experimental | Build recognized, gameplay mappings not fully verified |
| Earlier Retail builds | Upstream support | Depends on existing parser modules and opcode tables |

### PTR

**Published PTR release:** `ptr_12.1.7.70892_wpp`

The independent PTR WPP contains the original TrinityCore parser architecture, packet decoding, opcode mappings, version detection, and SQL generation.

Build `12.1.5.70961` registration and dispatch have been verified.

**PTR 12.1.7.70892 parsing compatibility has not yet been established through an authenticated capture.**

### Classic Era

The inherited upstream implementation contains registered client builds spanning 1.13.2 through 1.15.8, plus 1.60.1 beta-family registrations.

### Burning Crusade Classic

The inherited upstream implementation contains registered client builds spanning 2.5.1 through 2.5.6, including `2.5.6.70577`.

### Mists of Pandaria Classic

Includes the upstream 5.5.0–5.5.3 client registrations and relevant parser modules.

Known limitations include the `5.5.3.65703` version-dispatch omission and an upstream expansion-classification issue affecting some 5.5.x builds.

### WoW Forever

The separate Forever distribution is based on the Devorvh WowPacketParser fork and includes its additional Forever-specific parser module.

Its audited source contains 18 registered builds spanning 69876 through 70938.

**Forever remains standalone while compatibility work for the unified parser continues.**

